# WN22-AU-000090: Windows Server 2022 must be configured to audit Account Management - Other Account Management Events successes.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-au-000090-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 must be configured to audit Account Management - Other Account Management Events successes.`
    description `Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior. Other Account Management Events records events such as the a`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,audit-policy,medium,ksi-iam-jit,ksi-mla-let,ksi-mla-rvl`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-JIT,KSI:KSI-MLA-LET,KSI:KSI-MLA-RVL,NIST-800-53:AC-6(9),NIST-800-53:AU-12`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-JIT,KSI-MLA-LET,KSI-MLA-RVL`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Advanced Audit Policy Configuration >> System Audit Policies >> Account Management >> Audit Other Account Management Events with "Success" selected.`

    component_id `comp-windows-audit-policy`

    impl_KSI_IAM_JIT `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-JIT by enabling the 'Account Management >> Other Account Management Events' audit subcategory for success events via auditpol. The ESP scanner queries the subcategory via the windows_audit_policy CTN and fails the policy if the required success audit flag is not enabled. Remediation sets the subcategory via Group Policy (Advanced Audit Policy Configuration) or auditpol /set.`
    impl_KSI_MLA_LET `Windows Server implements KSI-MLA-LET by enabling the 'Account Management >> Other Account Management Events' audit subcategory for success events via auditpol. The ESP scanner queries the subcategory via the windows_audit_policy CTN and fails the policy if the required success audit flag is not enabled. Remediation sets the subcategory via Group Policy (Advanced Audit Policy Configuration) or auditpol /set.`
    impl_KSI_MLA_RVL `Windows Server implements KSI-MLA-RVL by enabling the 'Account Management >> Other Account Management Events' audit subcategory for success events via auditpol. The ESP scanner queries the subcategory via the windows_audit_policy CTN and fails the policy if the required success audit flag is not enabled. Remediation sets the subcategory via Group Policy (Advanced Audit Policy Configuration) or auditpol /set.`
    impl_AC_6_9 `Windows Server implements AC-6(9) by enabling the 'Account Management >> Other Account Management Events' audit subcategory for success events via auditpol. The ESP scanner queries the subcategory via the windows_audit_policy CTN and fails the policy if the required success audit flag is not enabled. Remediation sets the subcategory via Group Policy (Advanced Audit Policy Configuration) or auditpol /set.`
    impl_AU_12 `Windows Server implements AU-12 by enabling the 'Account Management >> Other Account Management Events' audit subcategory for success events via auditpol. The ESP scanner queries the subcategory via the windows_audit_policy CTN and fails the policy if the required success audit flag is not enabled. Remediation sets the subcategory via Group Policy (Advanced Audit Policy Configuration) or auditpol /set.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        subcategory `Other Account Management Events`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        success_audited boolean = true
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_audit_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
